<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<LanguageData>
  <!--EN: A simple chirashizushi bowl made from a few ingredients. In Chirashizushi rice is served in a bowl and topped with a variety of raw fish and vegetable garnishes. It is commonly eaten because it is filling, fast and easy to make.-->
  <VCE_Chirashizushi.description>用少许材料快速制作出的简单散寿司。散寿司，即将生鱼蔬菜等寿司材料盖在饭上。量足又制作简单。</VCE_Chirashizushi.description>
  <!--EN: chirashizushi bowl (simple)-->
  <VCE_Chirashizushi.label>散寿司（简单）</VCE_Chirashizushi.label>
  <!--EN: Sushi is one of the healthiest foods about. So sooner or later someone was going to deep fry it and make it the opposite. The end result is a crunchy, unhealthy yet tasty soul food - Not quite as filling as a meal, but very pleasing to eat. Deep frying sushi reduces shelf life as well unless frozen.-->
  <VCE_DeepFriedSushi.description>寿司是一种养生的食物，但是油炸后就未必了。它是一种香脆美味但不健康的食物。油炸食物不冷冻的话也会腐烂。</VCE_DeepFriedSushi.description>
  <!--EN: deep fried sushi-->
  <VCE_DeepFriedSushi.label>油炸寿司</VCE_DeepFriedSushi.label>
  <!--EN: A masterpiece of the culinary arts, this sushi nourishes the body, mind, and soul. Futomaki is a large cylindrical piece, usually with nori on the outside. A typical futomaki is five to six centimetres in diameter. They are often made with two, three, or more fillings that are chosen for their complementary tastes and colors.-->
  <VCE_Futomaki.description>厨艺界的大师级作品，这份寿司同时滋养了身体、思想和灵魂。太卷寿司，即用海苔包裹的大块柱状寿司。太卷寿司直径一般5-6cm。配料多种多样，塑造出复杂多变的外观和味道。</VCE_Futomaki.description>
  <!--EN: futomaki (lavish)-->
  <VCE_Futomaki.label>太卷寿司（奢侈）</VCE_Futomaki.label>
  <!--EN: A culinary work of art, characterized by refined, even elaborate preparation and presentation of an aesthetically balanced, albeit low quantity sushi. Gunkanmaki is a special type of nigirizushi: an oval, hand-formed clump of sushi rice that has a strip of nori wrapped around its perimeter to form a vessel that is filled with some soft, loose or fine-chopped ingredient that requires the confinement of nori such as roe.-->
  <VCE_Gunkanmaki.description>精雕细琢的寿司，美艳绝伦，虽然量不多。军舰卷寿司，即手捏海苔包裹椭圆柱状的饭团，米饭之上盛有一层松软的顶料。</VCE_Gunkanmaki.description>
  <!--EN: gunkanmaki (gourmet)-->
  <VCE_Gunkanmaki.label>军舰卷寿司（豪华）</VCE_Gunkanmaki.label>
  <!--EN: A nondistinct paste mimicking the texture of lobster, crab, or other shellfish. Only, this one... is made with human meat. A delicacy for cannibalistic Rim tribes, and a profoundly disgusting and taboo culinary experience for anyone else.-->
  <VCE_HumanSurimi.description>一种膏状食物，外表看上去与虾肉和蟹肉差不多，但这个。。。是用人肉做的，食人者的天堂，正常人的地狱。</VCE_HumanSurimi.description>
  <!--EN: human "surimi"-->
  <VCE_HumanSurimi.label>人肉膏</VCE_HumanSurimi.label>
  <!--EN: Complex nigiri sushi assembled with care from a wide selection of ingredients. Nigirizushi consists of an oblong mound of sushi rice that the chef presses between the palms of the hands to form an oval-shaped ball, and a topping (the neta) draped over the ball.-->
  <VCE_Nigiri.description>选择多种原料，精心制作出的一份相对复杂的握寿司。握寿司，即将长条形的米饭和配料用手握在一起定型成的寿司。</VCE_Nigiri.description>
  <!--EN: nigiri (fine)-->
  <VCE_Nigiri.label>握寿司（精致）</VCE_Nigiri.label>
  <!--EN: Simple norimaki sushi made from a few ingredients. Norimaki are a type of sushi wrapped with seaweed.-->
  <VCE_Norimaki.description>用少许材料快速制作出的卷寿司。卷寿司，即用紫菜包裹材料的寿司。</VCE_Norimaki.description>
  <!--EN: norimaki (simple)-->
  <VCE_Norimaki.label>卷寿司（简单）</VCE_Norimaki.label>
  <!--EN: A culinary work of art, characterized by refined, even elaborate preparation and presentation of an aesthetically balanced, albeit low quantity sushi. In oshizushi, a block-shaped piece is formed using a wooden mold. The chef lines the bottom of the mold with the toppings, covers them with sushi rice, and then presses the lid of the mold down to create a compact, rectilinear block. The block is removed from the mold and then cut into bite-sized pieces.-->
  <VCE_Oshizushi.description>精雕细琢的寿司，美艳绝伦，虽然量不多。押寿司，即原料层层叠加装在一个木盒里压制再切块制成的寿司。</VCE_Oshizushi.description>
  <!--EN: oshizushi (gourmet)-->
  <VCE_Oshizushi.label>押寿司（豪华）</VCE_Oshizushi.label>
  <!--EN: An edible bean that can be used as a vegetable in a multitude of recipes, and most famously known as the main ingredient in delicious soy sauce.-->
  <VCE_RawSoybean.description>有多种用途的可食用豆类植物。可以用来制作酱油。</VCE_RawSoybean.description>
  <!--EN: soybeans-->
  <VCE_RawSoybean.label>大豆</VCE_RawSoybean.label>
  <!--EN: A plant of the horseradish family. A paste made from its ground rhizomes is used as a pungent condiment for sushi and other foods. It is similar in taste to hot mustard rather than chili peppers in that it stimulates the nose more than the tongue.-->
  <VCE_RawWasabi.description>辣根科植物。其根部磨成的末可以用来调味寿司和其它食物。其辣味主要刺激呼吸道而不是舌头。</VCE_RawWasabi.description>
  <!--EN: wasabi-->
  <VCE_RawWasabi.label>山葵</VCE_RawWasabi.label>
  <!--EN: A soy fermenter is a cilindrical, metallic drum where soybeans are pressed, mixed with aspergillus bacteria and grain, and aged for long time periods. The result is soy sauce of increasing quality, which can be used as a food condiment.-->
  <VCE_SoyFermenter.description>一个圆柱状的金属发酵桶，其中大豆会被压制，和曲霉菌，谷物混合并发酵很长的一段时间。发酵时间越长，酱油质量越高。</VCE_SoyFermenter.description>
  <!--EN: soy sauce fermenter-->
  <VCE_SoyFermenter.label>酱油发酵桶</VCE_SoyFermenter.label>
  <!--EN: A fermented paste of soybeans, roasted grain, brine, and Aspergillus bacteria. Soy sauce can be added directly to food, and is used as a dip or salt flavor in cooking, as well as providing a rich umami taste.-->
  <VCE_SoySauce.description>大豆和曲霉，盐水，谷物一起发酵后制成的酱。烹饪加入食物可以提供鲜味。</VCE_SoySauce.description>
  <!--EN: soy sauce-->
  <VCE_SoySauce.label>酱油</VCE_SoySauce.label>
  <!--EN: A species of legume widely grown for its edible bean, which has numerous uses. Soybean plants grow quite fast, but they are very sensitive to temperature, with optimum growing conditions in mean temperatures of 20 to 30 °C (68 to 86 °F). Temperatures outside that range stunt growth significantly.-->
  <VCE_Soybean.description>有多种用途的可食用豆类植物。大豆生长很快但是对温度非常敏感，最佳生长环境是20至30 °C（68至86 °F）。在理想温度以外会大大减少生长速度。</VCE_Soybean.description>
  <!--EN: soybean plant-->
  <VCE_Soybean.label>大豆</VCE_Soybean.label>
  <!--EN: A working table to cut, slice and prepare all kinds of sushi.-->
  <VCE_SushiPrepTable.description>一个专门用来制备寿司的工作台。</VCE_SushiPrepTable.description>
  <!--EN: sushi prep table-->
  <VCE_SushiPrepTable.label>寿司制备台</VCE_SushiPrepTable.label>
  <!--EN: A masterpiece of the culinary arts, this sushi nourishes the body, mind, and soul. Temaki is a large cone-shaped piece of nori on the outside and the ingredients spilling out the wide end. A typical temaki is about 10 centimetres long, and is eaten with fingers because it is too awkward to pick it up with chopsticks.-->
  <VCE_Temaki.description>厨艺界的大师级作品，这份寿司同时滋养了身体、思想和灵魂。手卷寿司，即用一大片紫菜包裹住材料卷成的锥形寿司。手卷寿司一般有10cm左右长，通常用手拿着吃。</VCE_Temaki.description>
  <!--EN: temaki (lavish)-->
  <VCE_Temaki.label>手卷寿司（奢侈）</VCE_Temaki.label>
  <!--EN: Complex uramaki sushi assembled with care from a wide selection of ingredients. Uramaki is a medium-sized cylindrical piece with two or more fillings, and it differs from other maki because the rice is on the outside and the nori seaweed inside.-->
  <VCE_Uramaki.description>选择多种原料，精心制作出的一份相对复杂的反卷寿司。反卷寿司，即用米饭包裹紫菜和其它材料的一种中型寿司。</VCE_Uramaki.description>
  <!--EN: uramaki (fine)-->
  <VCE_Uramaki.label>反卷寿司（精致）</VCE_Uramaki.label>
  <!--EN: A plant of the horseradish family. A paste made from its ground rhizomes is used as a pungent condiment for sushi and other foods. It is similar in taste to hot mustard rather than chili peppers in that it stimulates the nose more than the tongue. Wasabi is widely considered to be one of the most difficult plants to grow, since it needs a temperate, extremely humid environment. It will receive a growth penalty if less than 20 tiles of water are found in a 6 tile radius.-->
  <VCE_Wasabi.description>辣根科植物。其根部磨成的末可以用来调味寿司和其它食物。其辣味主要刺激呼吸道而不是舌头。山葵种植非常困难，因为它对温度和湿度的要求都及其高。如果半径6格内有少于20格水的话生长速度会变慢。</VCE_Wasabi.description>
  <!--EN: wasabi plant-->
  <VCE_Wasabi.label>山葵</VCE_Wasabi.label>
  <!--EN: A paste made from ground wasabi rhizomes and used as a pungent condiment for sushi and other foods. It is similar in taste to hot mustard rather than chili peppers in that it stimulates the nose more than the tongue. It loses its flavour and deteriorates extremely fast.-->
  <VCE_WasabiPaste.description>用山葵根制成的末，可以用来调味寿司和其它食物。其辣味主要刺激呼吸道而不是舌头。老化速度非常快。</VCE_WasabiPaste.description>
  <!--EN: wasabi paste-->
  <VCE_WasabiPaste.label>芥末</VCE_WasabiPaste.label>
</LanguageData>
